@page "/docs/api-reference"
@layout DocsLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>API reference — Vaultex</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-eyebrow">API reference</div>
<h1>API reference</h1>
<p class="docs-lead">
    Vaultex exposes a standards-compliant OpenID Connect provider. Every endpoint is listed below
    with its parameters, request body, and response shape.
</p>

<h2 id="base-url">Base URL</h2>
<div class="docs-endpoint">
    <span>https://auth.vaultex.io</span>
</div>
<p>
    All endpoints are relative to this base URL. In a development environment Vaultex runs at
    <code>https://localhost:7108</code>.
</p>

<h2 id="endpoints">Endpoints</h2>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Endpoint</th><th>Method</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/api-reference/discovery">/.well-known/openid-configuration</a></td><td><span class="docs-method docs-method--get">GET</span></td><td>OIDC metadata document</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/api-reference/discovery">/.well-known/jwks</a></td><td><span class="docs-method docs-method--get">GET</span></td><td>Public signing keys</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/api-reference/authorize">/connect/authorize</a></td><td><span class="docs-method docs-method--get">GET</span></td><td>Start an authorization request</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/api-reference/token">/connect/token</a></td><td><span class="docs-method docs-method--post">POST</span></td><td>Exchange code or refresh token for access tokens</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/api-reference/userinfo">/connect/userinfo</a></td><td><span class="docs-method docs-method--get">GET</span></td><td>Read claims about the current user</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/api-reference/logout">/connect/logout</a></td><td><span class="docs-method docs-method--get">GET</span></td><td>End the user's session</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/docs/api-reference/revocation">/connect/revocation</a></td><td><span class="docs-method docs-method--post">POST</span></td><td>Revoke an issued token</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="auth">Authentication</h2>
<p>Endpoints that need client credentials accept them in two ways:</p>
<ul>
    <li><strong>HTTP Basic</strong> &mdash; <code>Authorization: Basic base64(client_id:client_secret)</code></li>
    <li><strong>Form post</strong> &mdash; <code>client_id</code> and <code>client_secret</code> as form fields</li>
</ul>
<p>Public clients (SPAs, mobile) don't have a secret. They send <code>client_id</code> and prove their identity with PKCE.</p>

<h2 id="errors">Error responses</h2>
<p>Errors follow the OAuth 2.0 / OIDC error format:</p>
<div class="docs-codeblock">
    <div class="docs-codeblock-header">
        <span class="docs-codeblock-lang">JSON</span>
        <button class="docs-codeblock-copy" onclick="vxCopy(this)">Copy</button>
    </div>
<pre><code>{
  "error": "invalid_grant",
  "error_description": "The authorization code has expired."
}</code></pre>
</div>
<p>See the <a href="/docs/errors">error reference</a> for every code Vaultex can return.</p>

